      "artist": "MagicRubberDuck",
      "description": "White Ladies Priory (or \"Whiteladies\") was once an Augustinian priory that was dedicated to St Leonard. It was founded in the late 12th century. Although it is not known exactly when the priory was built, the first known reference to the convent dates back to around 1186. As the nuns wore primarily white clothing, the priory became known as \"White Ladies\"; this also helped to distinguish the convent from the nearby Benedictine priory that was known as \"Black Ladies\". In 1651, Charles II took refuge at White Ladies Priory, before moving on to Boscobel House. The priory was officially dissolutioned in 1536.",
